                "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
                "senderName": "NWS Lubbock TX",
                "headline": "Flash Flood Warning issued October 14 at 6:31PM CDT until October 14 at 7:30PM CDT by NWS Lubbock TX",
                "description": "At 631 PM CDT, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms producing heavy\nrain across the warned area. Between 2 and 4 inches of rain have\nfallen. Additional rainfall amounts up to 1 inch are possible in the\nwarned area. Flash flooding is already occurring.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by thunderstorms.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor\ndrainage and low-lying areas.\n\nSome locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nSpur, Dickens, Clairemont and Justiceburg.",
                "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.",
                "response": "Avoid",
                "note": null,
