                "description": "FFWRLX\n\nThe National Weather Service in Charleston has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nSoutheastern Athens County in southeastern Ohio...\nSouthern Washington County in southeastern Ohio...\nWest Central Doddridge County in northern West Virginia...\nSouthwestern Tyler County in northern West Virginia...\nPleasants County in northwestern West Virginia...\nCentral Ritchie County in northwestern West Virginia...\nCentral Wood County in northwestern West Virginia...\n\n* Until 915 PM EDT.\n\n* At 622 PM EDT, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms producing\nheavy rain across the warned area. Between 1 and 2 inches of rain\nhave fallen. Additional rainfall amounts of 1 to 1.5 inches are\npossible in the warned area. Flash flooding is ongoing or expected\nto begin shortly.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by thunderstorms.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor\ndrainage and low-lying areas.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nParkersburg, Marietta, Belpre, Harrisville, St. Marys, Coolville,\nVienna, Williamstown, Pennsboro, Belmont, Boaz, North Bend State\nPark, Mineralwells, Lubeck, Washington, Newport, North Hills,\nEllenboro, Cairo and Pullman.\n\nThis includes the following highways...\nInterstate 77 in West Virginia between mile markers 170 and 186.\nInterstate 77 in Ohio between mile markers 1 and 3. Route 50 in West\nVirginia between mile markers 1 and 52.",
